--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components and how they affect what you may ship
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The core package - everything installed by `pip install dsdoctor` - depends
only on permissively licensed libraries (numpy, Pillow, PyYAML, rich, jinja2,
tqdm, and the OpenAI Python client). Nothing in the default install is
copyleft, and `dsdoctor scan`, `card`, `verify-card`, `recheck`, `diff`,
`resplit` and `convert` run entirely within that set.

The OPTIONAL `vision` extra (`pip install dsdoctor[vision]`) pulls in
Ultralytics, which is licensed under AGPL-3.0. AGPL obligations are
significant for network-deployed software. That extra exists only for
`model_disagreement_scan`, which is disabled by default and documented as
measured net-harmful (see README, iteration 4). Do not install the `vision`
extra unless you have decided that AGPL-3.0 is acceptable in your context.

`yolov8n.pt`, checked into this repository for reproducing that one retired
experiment, is an Ultralytics model file and is likewise AGPL-3.0.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

No dataset is redistributed by this repository. `eval/build_corpus.py`
downloads COCO 2017 annotations (CC BY 4.0) and val2017 images (Flickr-sourced,
under their original licences) at build time. See README, "Data provenance".
